.Dd $Mdocdate: April 30 2026 $
.Dt HMF 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmf
.Nd hide faces in an image by overlaying another image
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmf
.Fl i Ar input
.Fl o Ar output
.Fl f Ar face
.Op Fl m Ar model
.Op Fl t Ar threshold
.Op Fl p Ar percent
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
detects human faces in
.Ar input
using the YuNet DNN face detector and replaces each detected region
with
.Ar face ,
writing the resulting image to
.Ar output .
The replacement image is resized to match each face bounding box.
If
.Ar face
is a PNG with an alpha channel, transparency is honoured via per-pixel
alpha blending; otherwise the region is copied verbatim.
.Pp
YuNet is a small CNN
.Pq Pa face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx , approx. 230 KB
that ships separately from the OpenCV runtime.
It detects upright, profile, tilted, occluded and infant faces far more
reliably than the legacy Haar cascades, at the cost of a one-time model
download
.Pq see Sx FILES .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar input
Path to the source image.
Any format supported by OpenCV is accepted
.Pq JPEG, PNG, BMP, TIFF, WebP, ... .
.It Fl o Ar output
Path where the resulting image is written.
The encoder is selected from the file extension.
.It Fl f Ar face
Path to the replacement image.
A PNG with an alpha channel produces the cleanest blend.
.It Fl m Ar model
Path to the YuNet ONNX model.
Defaults to
.Pa /usr/local/share/hmf/yunet.onnx .
.It Fl t Ar threshold
Confidence threshold for accepting a detection, in
.Bq 0.0 , 1.0 .
Lower values keep more candidates at the risk of false positives.
The default is
.Cm 0.6 .
.It Fl p Ar percent
Grow each detected bounding box by
.Ar percent
of its width and height before overlaying, keeping the box centred on
the original detection.
Useful when the detector returns a tight crop and the replacement image
should also cover the forehead, chin or hair.
The default is
.Cm 0
.Pq no padding .
.It Fl v
Verbose mode.
Print the model path, image dimensions and the bounding box plus
confidence score of every detected face on standard error.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/hmf/yunet.onnx"
.It Pa /usr/local/share/hmf/yunet.onnx
Default location of the YuNet ONNX model.
Installed by
.Cm make install ,
which depends on the model being present in the source tree.
Run
.Cm make fetch-model
once before installing to download it from the OpenCV Model Zoo.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std hmf
.Pp
The program exits with status 1 if any of the input, output, face or
model files cannot be read or written, or if the command line is
malformed.
A run that succeeds but detects zero faces still exits with status 0;
the output image is written unchanged.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Replace every detected face in
.Pa group.jpg
with
.Pa mask.png ,
using the installed model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ hmf -i group.jpg -o anonymised.jpg -f mask.png
.Ed
.Pp
Run from a build tree, with verbose detection output and a lower
confidence threshold:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ hmf -v -t 0.4 -m ./yunet.onnx \\
    -i baby.jpg -o out.jpg -f mask.png
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mandoc 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The model file is not part of the
.Nm
source tree; fetch it with
.Cm make fetch-model
before
.Cm make install .
Heavy occlusion, motion blur or very low resolution can still cause
missed detections.
Lowering
.Fl t
helps recover marginal detections at the cost of false positives,
especially on busy backgrounds.
